        "thinking": "The server has `jsdom` as a production dependency. That causes `undici@7` to be pulled in when esbuild bundles the server code. The server uses `jsdom` for some DOM-parsing feature.\n\nNow, for the CF worker, this is a problem because `undici@7` contains `sqlite-cache-store.js` which requires `node:sqlite`, which is not available in the Workers runtime.\n\nThe best approach here is to:\n1. Mark `node:sqlite` and `@embedded-postgres/*` as external in the wrangler build\n\n\n2. Fix the `@paperclipai/db` dynamic import to avoid pulling in embedded-postgres\n\nI need to figure out how to configure Wrangler to mark these packages as external. Looking at the Wrangler documentation, I can use the build configuration in `wrangler.toml` to specify esbuild options including external packages.\n\nThe cleanest approach is to create a custom build script that Wrangler can invoke, where I can configure esbuild with the proper externals list. This way I can ensure `node:sqlite` and other problematic dependencies don't get bundled into the worker. I need to trace back where `jsdom` is actually being imported in the server code—it's likely a direct dependency of `better-auth` that's getting bundled when the worker pulls in the auth routes.",
